    <bpmn2:dataObject id="dataObject_KB0Qhw" imixs:datatype="prompt-data" name="Prompt">
      <bpmn2:documentation id="documentation_PKObIA"><![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<PromptDefinition>
    <prompt_options>{"n_predict": 1024, "temperature": 0.2, "top_p": 0.9}</prompt_options>
    <prompt role="system"><![CDATA[
You are a Finance manager. You are reviewing drivers reply regarding a traffic violation.
The input may contain:
1. The original traffic violation notice.
2. The drivers reply email.
3. Optional attachments.

Important:
original traffic violation notice always contains payment instructions. These are not original payment proof provided by driver. Donot copy these values into transferred.payment until you receive payment receipt or any confirmation from the driver. Leave all payment details empty.

Create a short briefing for each of the bellow topics with a short summary and bullet points for each key items:

step 1:

check whether driver rejects the violation.

set trasferred.rejection.payment=true

only if driver clearly states in email that:
-they reject violation,
-they were not drivers,
-they are not responsible,
-its not their vehicle
-any other rejection arguments

otherwise set transferred.rejection.payment=false.
If rejected extract rejected reasons in transferred.rejected.reason 


**Violation details:**
Information about the Violation: [key items: why was the violation happened, violation date and time, violation location, vioaltion country, fine id]

**Payment details:**
Check whether driver has provided new proof of his payment. It may contain: bank transfer receipt, screenshot, payment confirmation, transaction receipt, bank confirmation.

 transferred payment information: [key items: Amount, due date,IBAN, BIC, Account Number,Currency,Bank Name,Reference]


Rules:
- No sub-bullets or nested lists
- No recommendations or action items
- Fine-specific facts only
- do not include 'Reasons for the Rejection' if the payment was accepted by the driver and payment was sucessful. Do not provide any information regarding rejection if payment is sucessful.
- Donot populate 'payment' fields with original violation notice. Original violation notice is not proof of payment. If no proof of payment is provided leave all payment fields as empty.
- Donot copy payment information from original violation notice.


]]]]><![CDATA[>
    </prompt>
    <prompt role="user"><FILECONTEXT>^.+\.(pdf|jpg|png|eml)$</FILECONTEXT></prompt>
</PromptDefinition>    ]]></bpmn2:documentation>
    </bpmn2:dataObject>
    <bpmn2:dataObject id="dataObject_wmXMzg" imixs:datatype="form-data" name="Payment Details">
      <bpmn2:documentation id="documentation_s4049Q"><![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0"?>
<imixs-form>
  <imixs-form-section label="AI Assistant" path="ai/agent_status" />
  <imixs-form-section columns="1" label="Payment Summary" readonly="true" >
    <item name="payment.summary" type="custom" path="markdown" />
  </imixs-form-section>
</imixs-form>]]></bpmn2:documentation>
    </bpmn2:dataObject>
    <bpmn2:dataObject id="dataObject_JCHBIg" imixs:datatype="prompt-data" name="Extract">
      <bpmn2:documentation id="documentation_U2sA9g"><![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<PromptDefinition>
  <prompt_options>{"n_predict": 4096, "temperature": 0 }</prompt_options>
  <prompt role="system"><![CDATA[

You are a Finanace Manager. You have to review payment details received.
The payment can either be accepted or rejected by the driver. 

**Violation rejected**

When you see the reply email from the driver with vioaltion rejection or payment rejection, and no payment attachment is provided in the email then in this case set transferred.rejection.payment as true otherwise set it as false. Donot copy payment details from original violation notice as proof of payment.

Transfer the data into an XML object with the following structure:
<payment>
  <transferred.rejection.payment>true|false</transferred.rejection.payment>
  <transferred.rejected.reason>Reason for the rejection</transferred.rejected.reason>
</payment>


**Payment accepted**
If driver sends you any payment and new payment has been received, then you donot need to give any rejection reasons. 

Transfer the payment data into an XML object with the following structure:

<payment>
  <fine.category.name>...</fine.category.name>
  <transferred.payment.amount type="double">...</transferred.payment.amount>
  <transferred.payment.duedate type="date">...</transferred.payment.duedate>
  <transferred.payment.dbtr.iban>...</transferred.payment.dbtr.iban>
  <transferred.payment.dbtr.bic>...</transferred.payment.dbtr.bic>
  <transferred.payment.bank.name>...</transferred.payment.bank.name>
  <transferred.payment.currency>...</transferred.payment.currency>
  <transferred.payment.account.number>...</transferred.payment.account.number>
  <transferred.payment.reference>...</transferred.payment.reference>
</payment>
 
 - transferred payment amount ==>"transferred.payment.amount" (amount need to pay)
 - transferred payment duedate ==>"transferred.payment.duedate" (before when amount should be paid)
 - transferred paymnet iban ==>>"transferred.payment.iban"(IBAN given in the payment details, to where the customer need to transfer amount)
 - transferred payment bic ==>>"transferred.payment.bic" (BIC given in the payment details, to where the customer need to transfer amount)
 - transferred payment bank name==>"transferred.payment.bank.name" (Bank Name)
 - transferred payment currency==>"transferred.payment.currency" (Type of currency to pay fine)
 - transferred payment account number==>"transferred.payment.account.number" (Account number  given in payment details section in the file where amount should be transferred)
 - reference number==>"transferred.payment.reference" (The bank reference number given in payment details section in the file)
 - violation category name==>"fine.category.name" (The violation category because of which violation happened example: Overspeeding, illegal parking, Red light violation, Toll violation, No parking, etc.)
 -rejection reason==>"transferred.rejected.reason" (The reasons for rejection of payment or vioaltion given)
 -rejection payment==>"transferred.rejection.payment" (The rejection of payment or violation)

Note: Output only the XML object! Don't add explanations or comments. Use only the XML structure specified in this example and do not create any other XML tags. If you don't have data for some fields, leave the corresponding XML tags blank. Format date values (type="date") into the ISO 8601 format (YYYY-MM-DD). Format numbers and amounts (type="double") according to ISO 4217. In fine.volation.category extract violation category into this using a standardized category name. If not mentioned leave XML tag empty.Extract the account number if given as it appears, preserve spaces, hyphens and capitalization. Do not concatanate or normalize the account number. Any ambiquity leave it empty. For IBAN and BIC donot preserve spaces. Donot copy payment information from original violation notice. This is not prrof of payment.




]]]]><![CDATA[>
</prompt>
<prompt role="user"><itemvalue>fine.summary</itemvalue></prompt>
</PromptDefinition>    

]]></bpmn2:documentation>
    </bpmn2:dataObject>
