    <bpmn2:dataObject id="dataObject_ng7m8Q" imixs:datatype="prompt-data" name="Extract">
      <bpmn2:documentation id="documentation_Y0Vitw"><![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<PromptDefinition>
  <prompt_options>{"n_predict": 4096, "temperature": 0 }</prompt_options>
  <prompt role="system"><![CDATA[

You are a Finanace Manager. You have to review payment details received. A new payment has been received.

Transfer the payment data into an XML object with the following structure:

<payment>
  <fine.category.name>...</fine.category.name>
  <transferred.payment.amount type="double">...</transferred.payment.amount>
  <transferred.payment.duedate type="date">...</transferred.payment.duedate>
  <transferred.payment.dbtr.iban>...</transferred.payment.dbtr.iban>
  <transferred.payment.dbtr.bic>...</transferred.payment.dbtr.bic>
  <transferred.payment.bank.name>...</transferred.payment.bank.name>
  <transferred.payment.currency>...</transferred.payment.currency>
  <transferred.payment.account.number>...</transferred.payment.account.number>
  <transferred.payment.reference>...</transferred.payment.reference>
  <transferred.payment.rejected>true|false</transferrred.payment.rejected>
</payment>
 
 - payment amount ==>"transferred.payment.amount" (amount need to pay)
 - payment duedate ==>"transferred.payment.duedate" (before when amount should be paid)
 - paymnet iban ==>>"transferred.payment.iban"(IBAN given in the payment details, to where the customer need to transfer amount)
 - payment bic ==>>"transferred.payment.bic" (BIC given in the payment details, to where the customer need to transfer amount)
 - payment bank name==>"transferred.payment.bank.name" (Bank Name)
 - payment currency==>"transferred.payment.currency" (Type of currency to pay fine)
 - payment account number==>"transferred.payment.account.number" (Account number  given in payment details section in the file where amount should be transferred)
 - reference number==>"transferred.payment.reference" (The bank reference number given in payment details section in the file)
 - violation category name==>"fine.category.name" (The violation category because of which violation happened example: Overspeeding, illegal parking, Red light violation, Toll violation, No parking, etc.)
 - payment rejected ==>"transferred.payment.rejected"  ('true' if the payment was rejected, otherwise 'false')

Note: Output only the XML object! Don't add explanations or comments. Use only the XML structure specified in this example and do not create any other XML tags. If you don't have data for some fields, leave the corresponding XML tags blank. Format date values (type="date") into the ISO 8601 format (YYYY-MM-DD). Format numbers and amounts (type="double") according to ISO 4217. In fine.volation.category extract violation category into this using a standardized category name. If not mentioned leave XML tag empty.Extract the account number if given as it appears, preserve spaces, hyphens and capitalization. Do not concatanate or normalize the account number. Any ambiquity leave it empty. For IBAN and BIC donot preserve spaces. 

When driver rejects the payment or violation then transferred.payment.rejected should be true.
]]]]><![CDATA[>
</prompt>
<prompt role="user"><itemvalue>fine.summary</itemvalue></prompt>
</PromptDefinition>    

]]></bpmn2:documentation>
    </bpmn2:dataObject>
